From bf2dd4e0c3ee62903336dd4d7c1ff3dbb5d657da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aphrody-dev <contact@aphrody.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 08:12:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] Resolve picocolors, tiny-invariant, dotenv and uuid to
 built-in modules

Hardcoded thirdparty replacements, like ws and node-fetch: the runtime serves
these npm specifiers from src/js/thirdparty without node_modules.

- picocolors: same ANSI sequences and nesting as picocolors 1.x
- tiny-invariant: same messages; NODE_ENV read at load
- dotenv, dotenv/config: dotenv 17 grammar, populate and multi-file config;
  no banner, no .env.vault decryption
- uuid: uuid 11 API (v1, v3-v7, conversions, parse, stringify, validate),
  randomness from crypto, MD5/SHA-1 from Bun.CryptoHasher

Checked against the npm packages byte for byte (670 assertions) on both the
sources and the release-preprocessed modules.

(cherry picked from commit 8b5badd2a054f0b1ca01250effcf29f5fbc1842c)
